From b9c522d0563d7462b473edea69153130db27dc44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:30:23 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] info pages on CommandOutputKCM: inventory markers for the
 18 command-output pages (cpu, edid, egl, glx, vulkan, opencl, vaapi, wayland,
 xserver, kwinsupportinfo, pci, usb, network, interrupts, sensors,
 audio_information, block_devices, firmware_security)

These pages need nothing beyond the shared base (previous commit): each is a main.qml with CommandOutputKCM and a
CommandOutputContext in main.cpp; their look, busy indicator, filter, Refresh and error message all come from the base,
so they now look and behave the same. What this commit adds is only the `ksr: kcm_x/<row>` markers next to the
CommandOutputKCM item (Output, CopyToClipboard, Filter, FilterText, ReportError, PauseRefreshing on sensors), because the
rows' anchors are text only and the strict inventory check wants them in the page's own folder. No label, key, command or
argument changed, so nothing for ia/layout.json aliases. Relabel tables written in the outer repo (inventory/relabel).

Per page what it runs (unchanged): cpu lscpu --hierarchic=always; edid edid.sh; egl eglinfo; glx glxinfo; vulkan
vulkaninfo; opencl clinfo; vaapi vainfo; wayland wayland-info; xserver xdpyinfo; kwinsupportinfo qdbus KWin
supportInformation; pci lspci backend; usb lsusb -tv (auto refresh 1 s); network ip.sh (rich text); interrupts cat
/proc/interrupts (auto refresh not set); sensors sensors (1 s); audio_information pactl list; block_devices lsblk;
firmware_security fwupdmgr.sh (rich text). Wrap mode stays as it was (wrapping for cpu, audio, pci, wayland; tables do not
wrap).

Inventory: --strict 0 lost for each of the 18. Speed: see base commit (tool now started after page creation). Remaining
cost not fixed: the output goes into one Kirigami.SelectableLabel, so a very long output (vulkaninfo, glxinfo, clinfo)
lays out its whole text on the GUI thread when it arrives. Not built yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
